    "colour": {
      "describes": "The colour still (Øystein, 28 October: one in p2, the one exception to clay-first): only hue and chroma, laid on the clay's own L*, so the clay and colour stills share their values. Each colour is [C, h], CIE LCh: a material's at its own clay L* (its paint, bare fibre, under layer and stain at their values; the wash at the paint's less `tongue.washL`), turned to a tint of luminance 1, so its albedo keeps the clay's luminance; a light's as it reads alone on a neutral white at `atL`, its strength the clay's; the plain sky behind (`background`) at its clay L*, the third number, and the ground (`floor`) at `ground.L`. Muted all over; true colour only where people keep things, and 107 is not kept. Shade and ambient take the light's colour, never the object's (VD2).",
