    "tongue": {
      "describes": "The one failed-paint shape, following the water: off the sill's ends (the leaking one most) to the plinth, and down beside the casing from the head's leaking end. Its wash is soft and darker, water and dirt: on each board it spreads toward the drip edge, where the water lingers, and the board below takes it narrower again. Its peel is hard and darker, bare timber gone grey and holding the wet (the material's `bareL`), that keeps only `bareWash` of the wash: strips along the grain up from each board's drip edge, their tops torn in steps, highest at a butt joint. Each board's share of both is its own, so no mark crosses a lap. A run's `peel` lists [width, height] shares for its faces from the top down, the drip board's last.",
      "washL": 18, "bareWash": 0.12, "soft": 0.03,
      "runoff": { "describes": "The water's runs, obeying the wood (p3, the cold critic's change, in place of the soft runs below and `sillWash`): off each of the sill's horns, and off each batten's lower end, where its tilt sends the water, one narrow streak `inset` in from the end, down `boards` laps, `width` [m, first to last lap] times `scale`; over each lap's lowest `dripMm`, where the water hangs, its body is soft, `core` of its half-width dark, a `neck` of its width under the lap above spreading (`spread`, a power) to the whole at the drip edge, its wash darkening from `L`[0] to `L`[1] there and `fade` lighter by its last lap; its edges wobble by `wobble`; over the drip edge's lowest `dripMm` a hard tick, `tick` of its width, the cladding's `stainDL` darker still; each lap turns it by up to `wander`. From the street stop on (the stroke mips `far.lod`) each run is one soft mark of its own: `far.width` times as wide, `far.L` dark, `far.core` of it full. With `tonguePeel` the tongue's peel stays below, and with `tongueWash` its wash. At the last drip edge a hard-edged flake of bare wood (`bareL`), lifted along the grain, `flake` [width m, share of the face], torn as the peel is.", "use": true,
